    "note": [
     {
      "text": "47-year-old female presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 3 weeks. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 3/10. Associated: blurred vision, weight loss, tiredness. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 5 years; Hypertension for 4 years; Appendectomy in 2015. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: no similar illness. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
     }
